  cites Foreword chapter Console

Section: A Card Nothing Reaches

 The refused send returns before any queue is polled and before any frame
 is flushed, so the device record only has to exist. Every base address
 here is zero, and a poll through it answers "no frame" forever rather
 than faulting, which is why the connection is closed as well: a drain
 that ran anyway would spend its whole fuel cap instead of ending the arm.

  dead-pci : Arm64PciDevice = Arm64PciDevice { pci-bus = 0, pci-dev = 0, pci-func = 0, pci-vendor = 0, pci-device-id = 0, pci-class = 0, pci-subclass = 0, pci-header-type = 0 }
  dead-dev : VirtioDevice = VirtioDevice { pci-dev = dead-pci, common-base = 0, notify-base = 0, notify-off-multiplier = 0, isr-base = 0, device-cfg-base = 0 }
  dead-q : VirtqueueState = VirtqueueState { desc-base = 0, avail-base = 0, used-base = 0, queue-size = 0, free-head = 0, avail-idx = 0, last-used-idx = 0, notify-addr = 0 }
  dead-vnet : VirtioNetState = VirtioNetState { device = dead-dev, rx-queue = dead-q, tx-queue = dead-q, mac = [82, 84, 0, 18, 52, 86] }

Section: A Session With No Room Left

  cli-mac : List Integer = [82, 85, 10, 0, 2, 2]
  cli-ip : List Integer = [10, 0, 2, 100]
  srv-ip : List Integer = [10, 0, 2, 15]
  gw-ip : List Integer = [10, 0, 2, 2]

  seg0 : RexmitSeg = RexmitSeg { rx-frame = [], rx-ack = 0, rx-sent = 0, rx-resent = False }

  fill-queue : Integer, List RexmitSeg -> List RexmitSeg
  fill-queue (n) (acc) = if n <= 0 then acc else fill-queue (n - 1) (list-push acc seg0)

  base-sess : NetSession = net-session-new cli-mac cli-ip gw-ip 50000 80 srv-ip 1000

  stalled : NetSession =
    let closed = set-conn base-sess (tcp-set-state (base-sess.conn) TcpClosed)
    in set-rexmit closed (fill-queue net-rexmit-capacity []) 3 0

Section: Payload

  mk-bytes : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  mk-bytes (n) (acc) = if n <= 0 then acc else mk-bytes (n - 1) (list-push acc 65)

  payload-len : Integer = 50000

Section: Entry

 A refused send that advances anyway slices every chunk it walks past, so
 the cost of the call is the count of chunks it tried. Measured 2026-08-10
 by removing the guard: 593,152 bytes against 16,400 for the one slice a
 stop pays. The threshold is 44,800, which is 2.7x above the stopping arm
 and 13x below the walking one, so neither sits near it.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let data = mk-bytes payload-len []
    in let st0 = Arm64NetIOState { vnet = dead-vnet, transport = transport-new stalled }
    in let chunks = payload-len / arm64-net-mss
    in act
      print-line-uni ("queued=" & show (list-length ((st0.transport).session).rexmit-queue) & " full=" & show (net-rexmit-full ((st0.transport).session)))
      print-line-uni ("chunks-if-it-walks=" & show chunks)
      let h0 = __heap-save
      in let st1 = arm64-net-io-send-chunk st0 data 0 payload-len
      in let used = __heap-save - h0
      in act
        print-line-uni ("sent-anything=" & show (list-length (((st1.transport).session).outbox) > 0))
        print-line-uni ("stopped-at-first-refusal=" & show (used < arm64-net-mss * 8 * 4))
      end
    end
  end
